The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (open_flags & O_CREAT) {
    error = nfs_do_create(dir, dentry, mode, open_flags);
}
```
Reason:
The `nfs_atomic_open_v23` function does not check the length of the file name (`dentry->d_name.len`) before calling `nfs_do_create()`. If the file name exceeds `NFS3_MAXNAMLEN`, it results in a warning in `encode_filename3()` instead of returning an appropriate error, leading to undefined behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (dentry->d_name.len > NFS_SERVER(dir)->namelen)
    return -ENAMETOOLONG;
```
Reason:
This added check ensures that if the file name length exceeds the maximum allowed length (`NFS3_MAXNAMLEN`), the function will return an `-ENAMETOOLONG` error code before proceeding with any file operations, thus preventing the warning and handling the error gracefully.

